{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>Like the appearance of tzara'at of the skin of the flesh.</b> Like the appearance of the tzara'at stated in the section of ״עוֹר בָּשָׂר״ — ״אָדָם כִּי יִהְיֶה בְעוֹר בְּשָׂרוֹ״ — and what is stated about it? That it defiles in four appearances, and is evaluated for two weeks; and not like the appearance of tzara'at stated in a boil or a burn, which is evaluated for one week, and not like the appearance of nettles in a place of hair, which do not defile in four appearances — שְׂאֵת and its derivative, בַּהֶרֶת and its derivative."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:15.528128427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}